{"id": "EUVD-2026-103815", "enisaUuid": "cc4b4e4e-2c3b-3f8d-95fb-60816caef7e9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: btintel_pcie: reject oversized TX packets in send_frame()\n\nbtintel_pcie_send_frame() eventually copies skb->data into a fixed\nBTINTEL_PCIE_BUFFER_SIZE (4096) DMA buffer via memcpy() in\nbtintel_pcie_prepare_tx(), with a 4-byte PCIe type header prepended.\nA user-space process with HCI_CHANNEL_USER access can inject an\noversized packet and overflow the buffer.\n\nReject packets larger than\nBTINTEL_PCIE_BUFFER_SIZE - BTINTEL_PCIE_HCI_TYPE_LEN on entry.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:24:40", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d6ba6be9bef13edcd4ad74f7cfdd0c34db4d2bc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/84df222de86eabed543361025ed54ce838c0b573", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9806a748f9ab223b733624367b6ddda77fb9450e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f771f96557a4d953a7e4d045870547271e36e819"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98730", "GHSA-3249-w698-6rq3"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "19a30cc7-9ac8-32d1-84fa-f3fc12bbca1a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2bcb75f4-c6eb-3332-be15-7a5d70993581", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10"}, {"id": "337fe00d-a83f-3b02-8f11-e2a1e70db2b6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6e65a09f927566f257322358d429b267548473eb <84df222de86eabed543361025ed54ce838c0b573"}, {"id": "3843db5c-9a1b-3a3f-9e03-898e87edc0e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8ed80c49-7ace-32e9-b27e-e216d97485fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6e65a09f927566f257322358d429b267548473eb <9806a748f9ab223b733624367b6ddda77fb9450e"}, 